3.0 IMPACT DOMAINS
3.1 Terrestrial Impacts
3.1.1 Soil Chemistry
pH Impact: Neutral (±0.3 pH units) - calcium polyphosphate buffers to neutral

Nutrient Loading: Equivalent to light fertilizer application (3-5 kg P/ha) - beneficial in fire-affected soils

Metals/Contaminants: No heavy metals above detection limits (tested)

Salinity: Negligible increase (<10 µS/cm)

Microbial Impact: Transient shift (7-14 days) to phosphate-degrading microbes, returns to baseline

3.1.2 Vegetation Impacts
Direct Coating: Gel adheres but allows 85-90% PAR transmission

Gas Exchange: CO₂/O₂ exchange reduced by 15-20% for 24-48 hours

Long-term Effects: No phytotoxicity observed at 2× field concentration

Seed Germination: No inhibition at field rates; slight enhancement in some species

