3.2.2 Worst-case Scenario Analysis
Assuming accidental direct water impact:

Acute Toxicity: LC50 >100 mg/L for all aquatic test species

Eutrophication Potential: 12kg phosphate per unit = equivalent to 0.2 ha agricultural runoff

Oxygen Demand: BOD5 = 150 mg/L (moderate, dissipates in 5-7 days)

Mitigation: Rapid dilution (1:1000 in 1 hour in flowing water)

3.3 Atmospheric Impacts
3.3.1 Blast Effects
Overpressure: <0.5 psi at 100m, <0.1 psi at 500m

Noise: 125 dB at 100m (equivalent to jet takeoff)

Duration: <1 second impulse

Shockwave Propagation: Ground-level only, no stratospheric effects

3.3.2 Particulate Matter
PM10 Generation: 0.5-1.0 kg per unit (soil/organic dust)

Dispersion: Within 30 minutes at wind speed >2 m/s

Chemical Composition: Soil minerals + biodegradable polymers

