3.4 Biological Impacts
3.4.1 Fauna (Terrestrial)
Direct Blast Risk: Limited to <50m radius (no deployment in occupied areas)

Noise Disturbance: Temporary displacement (<24 hours) within 500m

Habitat Modification: Gel degrades before significant habitat alteration

Food Chain Effects: No biomagnification potential

3.4.2 Avian Specific Assessment
In-flight Collision Risk: Equivalent to other aerial operations

Nesting Disruption: No deployment within 1km of known raptor nests

Acute Stress: Comparable to thunderstorm exposure

3.4.3 Soil Biota
Microbial Communities: Transient shift, recovery within 14 days

Earthworms/Arthropods: No mortality at field concentrations

Root Zone Effects: No penetration beyond top 5cm soil layer

3.4.4 Sensitive/Protected Species Protocol
text
SPECIES-SPECIFIC PROTECTIONS:
1. California Condor (Gymnogyps californianus)
   - No deployment within 5km of nesting sites
   - No deployment during breeding season (Jan-July)
   
2. Spotted Owl (Strix occidentalis)
   - 1km buffer from known territories
   - Night operations prohibited in habitat
   
3. Desert Tortoise (Gopherus agassizii)
   - Visual survey required within 100m
   - No deployment if tortoise observed
   
4. Salmonid Streams
   - 500m buffer during spawning season
   - Downwind drift monitoring required
